@* Purpose: Home page of the application.

What it does

This is the first page the user sees.

It usually explains:

what the app is
what it is for
where to go next
Why it exists

Gives the user a landing page and context.


    Views

This is the UI.

These are .cshtml files.

Each controller usually has a matching folder inside Views.

Example structure:

Views
├── Home
├── Items
├── Account
└── Shared

What views do:

display HTML pages
show forms
show lists of data
show details pages

Example:
Views/Items/Index.cshtml shows the list of items.
